# /etc/cis-audit/exceptions.conf  (copy from etc/exceptions.conf.example)
#
# Accepted deviations, one per line:
#   id | justification | approved_by | expires (YYYY-MM-DD)
#
# - Exactly three '|' separators; no '|' inside the text.
# - The id must exist in the catalog, otherwise the run stops with exit code 3.
# - An exception only turns a FAIL into EXCEPTION. It never changes ERROR or MANUAL.
# - After the expiry date the control is reported as FAIL again, with a note.
# - A control that passes although an exception exists keeps PASS and a note
#   "exception no longer needed".

2.1.19 | Host is the production web server (nginx on 80/443) | V. Hoeck | 2027-10-31
